# shellcheck configuration for llmstack-ubuntu.sh and tests/unit.sh
#
# CI runs plain `shellcheck -x` on both files, so this file is the only lint
# configuration and a local run behaves exactly like CI.
#
# No checks are disabled globally. Known false positives are suppressed at
# the exact line, where the reason sits next to the code:
#
#   SC2016  STATUS_BODY and the llm* command templates are single-quoted on
#           purpose: expansion happens later, when the command runs. The
#           tests disable it file-wide because check() evaluates its
#           argument later.
#   SC1091  `source=/dev/null` on the config file, which is written at
#           install time and cannot be followed statically.
#
# Only add a global `disable=` here for a code that fires across the whole
# file, with a comment explaining why it is a false positive. A global
# disable hides every future instance, including real bugs.

# Follow `source` directives without needing -x on every invocation.
external-sources=true
